5a.  AN EXACT FLAT DIRECTION, PROVEN: kappa and the FOOTING are one column, not two
=========================================================================================================
  max |S[:,kappa] - S[:,footing]| over all 7 fronts = 0.000e+00
   [OK] kappa and the footing choice (rho_DE/cH_Lambda vs rho_total/cH_0) enter EVERY front only through their product a0.  The two columns agree to 0.0e+00, so the direction d ln kappa = -d ln footing is EXACTLY flat: no combination of these seven fronts can separate 'kappa = 1/2 on the canonical footing' from 'kappa = 1/2/1.2082 on the ALT footing'.  This is one guaranteed unit of irreducible dof, and it is a THEOREM about the fronts, not a precision limit
  the ALT/canon ratio is 1/sqrt(Omega_Lambda) = 1.2085 = 0.0822 dex, and the framework's OWN kappa signal against Milgrom 2020's 1/2pi is 0.0356 dex -- the footing fork is 2.3x LARGER than the number it is meant to measure

