  COST TO WIDE BINARIES: gamma_v 1.1114 -> 1.0758 (-1.783 sigma_sys) -- the ONE front that notices, and only at 1.78 sigma
   [OK] even the wide-binary target moves only 1.78 sigma_sys when alpha goes 1 -> 1.26, which is below the 3-sigma threshold that sigma_sys = 0.02 already caps at 1.55 sigma anyway

  *** VERDICT ON Q4, both halves. ***
  YES, ONE SHAPE DOF IS REMOVED BY OVER-DETERMINATION, in the exact sense asked: the solar
  system FIXES alpha >= 1.26, and SPARC (0.0014 dex), clusters
  (0.0055 dex) and even the wide-binary forecast (1.78 sigma) all accept it.  Six orders of magnitude in acceleration
  separate the two fronts, and they are compatible.  That is the one clean scale bridge here.
  AND WHAT IT COSTS, which must be said in the same breath: alpha = 1 is not a modelling
  choice in this framework, it is the EXACT LAW g_obs^2 = g_bar^2 + a0 g_bar (Sec. 1 proves the
  identity) and it is Milgrom 1999 eq 9, the kernel the dS-Unruh construction hands over.
  Buying alpha >= 1.26 therefore does not reduce the dof count by one -- it converts
  a CONSTRAINED shape dof into an UNEXPLAINED kernel choice.  Net: the fit loses a parameter,
  the theory loses a derivation.  The word 'exact' must be withdrawn either way.

