9.  THE FINAL HONEST DOF COUNT, AND EVERY REMAINING FLAT DIRECTION
=========================================================================================================
  NOMINAL free quantities enumerated (none removed): 7
     1. ln kappa               seen by 5 front(s)  [OVER-DETERMINED]
     2. ln footing             seen by 5 front(s)  [OVER-DETERMINED]
     3. ln omega_c             seen by 1 front(s)  [FITTED (1 front)]
     4. alpha                  seen by 3 front(s)  [OVER-DETERMINED]
     5. delta (I_0 x f_cl)     seen by 0 front(s)  [UNCONSTRAINED]
     6. ln xi_EFE              seen by 4 front(s)  [OVER-DETERMINED]
     7. f (a0z floor)          seen by 1 front(s)  [FITTED (1 front)]

  PHYSICAL RANK of the 7x7 sensitivity matrix (sv >= 1 sigma) = 5
  IN-HAND rank, dropping the un-measured wide-binary row       = 5
  -> IRREDUCIBLE FREE DOF = 7 - 5 = 2 (and 2 counting the DR4 forecast)

  THE FLAT DIRECTIONS, named and explained:
   1. d ln kappa = -d ln(footing).  EXACTLY flat, proven in 5a to 1e-12: every front sees
      kappa and the footing only through a0.  The footing fork is 2.3x larger than the kappa signal it would measure.
   2. delta = I_0 x f_clustered.  UNCONSTRAINED by all seven fronts.  The only front that could
      see it needs delta = 4.5 (the LambdaCDM dark-matter amount) and the
      framework's own particle-vs-mode position sets f_clustered = 0.  Zeroed BY POSTULATE.
   3. f, the a0(z) floor choice.  Seen by ONE front (F5), which is itself LambdaCDM-degenerate
      and currently CONTESTED (MUSE-DARK III measures a0 rising).  One front = a fit.

  WHAT DID GET BRIDGED, and it is not nothing:
   * alpha, the shape dof: the ephemeris FIXES it at >= 1.26 and SPARC (0.0014 dex),
     clusters (0.0055 dex) and the WB forecast all accept -- six orders of magnitude bridged.
     But the price is the exact law and the Milgrom-1999 kernel, so this trades a fitted
     parameter for an unexplained one rather than reducing the total.
   * a0: SPARC orbital FREQUENCIES + LLR give a0 <= 1.161e-10 with no RAR fit in it --
     a second, methodologically disjoint line.  It clears canon by 24.0% and ALT by 2.6%.
   * omega_c: the two edges are compatible with only 16.4% of the LLR-permitted
     log-range surviving, so the consistency test is real and it passed -- but a one-sided
     upper bound cannot imply a lower bound, so nothing was derived.  And no natural scale in
     the framework lands in the window.

  ENGAGING THE PRIOR RESULT.  The 2026-06-15 analysis found the framework jointly viable on
  8 of 9 fronts at +2 degrees of freedom with zero referee-proof kills.  This lane's answer to
  'can those +2 be driven to 0 by over-determination' is NO, and it says which two survive and
  why: the kappa-footing product (a theorem about the fronts) and the ghost-condensate amount
  (zeroed by the framework's own postulate).  Sec. 8 independently reproduces the 'zero
  referee-proof kills' half -- the best joint point sits at 1.15 sigma worst-front.

  OUTCOME: (c) CONTINUUM / DEGENERATE.  Not (a): the parameters are not derived.  Not (b): no
  front pair is mutually exclusive.  The dof count cannot be driven to zero by these fronts,
  and the reason is structural in two of the three cases, not a matter of precision.
  NO DOOR IS DECLARED CLOSED.  What would change the answer: (i) a front that sees kappa other
  than through a0 -- i.e. a prediction of Z, not of a0; (ii) any observable sensitive to the
  condensate amount without a free clustered fraction; (iii) a second, independent a0(z) front.

